audio.cpp fork deltas on the CUDA/HIP backend, captured 2026-09-23. They reached
external/ggml through audio.cpp merges WITHOUT a tracked patch, so the next
sync-ggml.sh run would have deleted them silently (see the patch-invariant note
in external/ggml/UPSTREAM). Source commits (audio.cpp PR numbers):

  - #321 (69421fc9) per-backend CUDA stream priority and stream access:
      ggml_backend_cuda_set_stream_priority(backend, priority) - lazily created
      streams use cudaStreamCreateWithPriority when priority != 0; streams that
      already exist keep theirs. ggml_backend_cuda_get_stream(backend) returns
      the compute cudaStream_t so host code can order its own kernels/copies
      with graph computes. Both are exported through the reg proc-address
      table; the engine resolves them dynamically in
      src/framework/core/backend.cpp (used by yue2, fish_audio and the qwen
      decode runtime). Also: ggml_backend_cuda_clear_graph's definition spells
      "struct ggml_cgraph", matching the C header declaration from patch 0007.
  - #320 (17751c0e) zero the MMQ stream-k fixup staging buffer before launch.
      The fixup pass reads tiles a partial block may not have written; without
      the memset those are uninitialised pool memory (nondeterministic output
      on reused pool capacity).
  - #346 (ee7be933) vendors/hip.h: the CUDA -> HIP name mapping the above needs.

Both new entry points tolerate a NULL backend, matching 0007's hooks.

Rebased onto ggml 0.24.0 (456172ec) on 2026-09-23, on top of the new 0007
(transcribe.cpp's implementation): the two declarations now follow 0007's
documented trim/evict block in include/ggml-cuda.h.

Not carried: the audio.cpp tree also re-declared
ggml_backend_cuda_split_buffer_type in include/ggml-cuda.h. Upstream has no
definition for it and nothing in this repo calls it - a stale header line left
by a merge - so it is intentionally dropped.

Retire each hunk when upstream ggml grows an equivalent (the MMQ memset is a
good upstream-PR candidate).

